 # Batch Chorus and Tattler interim messages outside Pi steering queue
 
-Problem 1: if multiple Chorus/Tattler messages arrive while an agent is working, Pi steering queue mode one-at-a-time serializes them, so the agent may see only the oldest interim message before responding and the rest later. Source correction: one-at-a-time drains the oldest queued message, not the most recent. Extensions cannot set steeringMode/followUpMode or edit the queue through public ExtensionAPI; they can only enqueue via sendMessage/sendUserMessage deliverAs and see ctx.hasPendingMessages(). No-upstream mitigation: keep an extension-owned pending inbox keyed by roomId/postId while busy, render live in widget, and flush one batched custom message once idle so the Pi queue sees a single catch-up item containing the burst.
+Updated design: Tattler, not Chorus, should own a durable pending inbox for inbound messages that arrive while an agent is busy. Inbound while busy goes to Tattler-owned pending inbox keyed by message/room/post IDs, not Pi steer/followUp. before_agent_start becomes the canonical drain point for any next turn (user prompt, model cooperative receive, normal continuation): if pending exists, inject one persistent custom batch message into that new turn, then clear/mark delivered only after injection succeeds. This also handles user abort + resume: abort may kill the provider stream, but not Tattler inbox; the next prompt drains missed messages. Batch custom message should use content for model-visible concatenated messages and details.kind=batch with structured messages array for custom rendering as individual blocks.
 
